course: dictionary
lesson: 4189
title: Good and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Good is a small word that does a big job. It can praise how well something is made, how kind someone is, or how well they behave. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Look at «a good drawing» and «a good person». In the first, good means well done. In the second, it means kind and honest. Ask yourself: is the word describing a thing or a person?
explain: Good also appears in phrases such as «good at maths», «good for you» and «for good». Each phrase has its own meaning, so learn it as one chunk. Good can also be a noun: «goods» means things that are made and sold.
explain: Sometimes people mean the opposite of what they say. «That's not the worst idea you've had» is a dry way of saying «good idea». A smile or a warm tone can show the real meaning, so use context to check.
fact: «Good» can mean of high quality or done well, as in «a good drawing».
fact: «Good» can mean kind, right and honest, as in «a good person».
fact: «Good» can mean healthy or helpful, as in «Vegetables are good for you.»
fact: «Goods» (with an s) means things that are made and sold.
fact: «Good at» means able to do something well, and «for good» means forever.
exercise: «Vegetables are good for you.» What does good mean here? | Tasty and sweet | Loud and noisy | *Healthy and helpful | Very old
exercise: Maya says, «Ben is good at maths.» What does good at mean? | Good at sport | *Able to do maths well | Always late for maths | Bored of maths
exercise: The shop sells «goods» like shoes and bags. What are goods? | *Things that are made and sold | Good days for shopping | Rules about being good | Good people who work in the shop
test: In «a good time at the party», good means: | Healthy and helpful | *Pleasant or enjoyable | Made of high quality wood | Behaving well
test: «That's not the worst idea you've had» is a dry way of saying: | A bad idea | *A good idea | An idea nobody will hear | The worst idea ever
exam: Which meaning of good fits «Be good while I am out»? | Of high quality | *Behaving well | Things to sell | Able to do something well
